$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for lithiation of
cis-stilbene followed by electrophile reaction. A solution of
cis-stilbene (250 mg, 1.38 mmol) and PMDTA (240 mg, 1.38 mmol) in THF
(17.3 mL) was cooled to -25 ºC and treated dropwise with sec-butyllithium
(2.76 mmol) over 5 minutes. The reaction mixture was stirred at -25 ºC
for a further 2 h and treated with the relevant electrophile. The flask
was allowed to warm to rt, hydrochloric acid (2 M, 1 mL) added and the
THF removed under reduced pressure. The residue was extracted with CH2Cl2
(3 x 10 mL), washed with hydrochloric acid (2 M, 1.0 mL). The organic
layer was dried over sodium sulfate and concentrated to dryness.
(Z)-1,2,3-Triphenyl-prop-2-en-1-ol (7). Benzaldehyde (5 equiv.) used as
electrophile. Purified by silica gel chromatography eluting with
pentane:diethyl ether (9:1) yielded a colorless solid which was
recrystallized from cyclohexane/diethyl ether (9:1) to fully purify (296
mg, 75%), mp 99-100 °C, (lit. mp1 100-101 °C). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
2.10 (1H, d, J = 6.6 Hz), 6.18 (1H, d, J = 6.6 Hz), 7.01 (1H, s),
7.22-7.45 (15H, m). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 71.5, 126.3, 127.3, 127.6,
127.7, 128.3, 128.6, 128.7, 128.8, 129.0, 132.2, 136.9, 139.6, 142.5,
142.9. IR (KBr disc): 3313, 3255, 1492 cm-1. ES-MS: m/z 285.2 [M - H]-.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development and Application of a Direct Vinyl Lithiation of cis-Stilbene
and a Directed Vinyl Lithiation of an Unsymmetrical cis-Stilbene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cotter, Juliet; Hogan, Anne-Marie L.; O'Shea, Donal F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(8), 1493-1496

