$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (±)-1-(3',4'-Diacetoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol
(1g). A stirred solution of 3,4-diacetoxybenzaldehyde (1 g, 4.5 mmol) and
allyl iodide (0.41 mL, 4.5 mmol) in water (100 mL) was treated with
indium powder (0.52g, 4.5 mmol). The solution was stirred vigorously for
48 h and then extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 100 mL). The combined
organic extracts were washed with water (2 x 50 mL) and brine (50 mL),
and dried (MgSO4). The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to
yield the crude product which was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel eluting with ethyl acetate in hexane to yield alcohol 1g as a
pale yellow oil (1.09 g, 92%): (±)-1-(3'-Fluorophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1d).
(99% yield): Other (±)-1-arylbut-3-en-1-ols (1a-f) were prepared in
analogous manner. All have been synthesised previously by other routes
such as Grignard addition to the corresponding aldehydes. silica gel TLC
Rf 0.33 (25% ethyl acetate-hexane); Spectral data in agreement with
published data.4
