$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Chloro-α-(2-propenyl)benzenemethanol, 2g (Table 2, entry 7). An
oven-dried 25 mL round bottom flask was cooled under argon and charged
with (1S,2R)-(+)-2-amino-1,2-diphenylethanol (0.213 g, 1 mmol), indium
powder (0.114 g, 1 mmol), anhydrous THF (7 mL), anhydrous pyridine (0.08
mL, 1 mmol) and allyl bromide (0.084 mL, 1 mmol). The mixture was stirred
vigorously at 25 °C for 30 min, at which time n-hexane (1 mL) was added,
the solution cooled to -78 °C (dry ice/acetone bath), and freshly
distilled 3-chlorobenzaldehyde (0.057 mL, 0.5 mmol) was added dropwise.
After 2 h the reaction was quenched with saturated ammonium chloride (1
mL) and allowed to warm to 25 °C. Deionized water was added and the
mixture extracted with n-hexane (2 x 3 mL), the combined organic layers
were dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered through a small
plug of silica gel and evaporated to give a clear, colorless oil (0.082
g, 90% yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.17 (s, 1H, OH), 2.38-2.57 (m,
2H) 4.71 (dd, J = 5.25 and 7.75 Hz, 1H) 5.14-5.21 (m, 1H), 5.71-5.87 (m,
1H), 7.16-7.36 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz, CDCl3): δ 43.7, 72.5, 118.8,
123.9, 125.9, 127.5, 129.6, 133.8, 134.9, 145.8. Enantiomeric excess was
determined to be 80% by chiral GC analysis. GC conditions: 151 °C
isothermal; tR for the (R)-alcohol: 36.08 min, tR for the (S)-alcohol:
36.69 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indium-Mediated Asymmetric Barbier-Type Allylations: Additions to
Aldehydes and Ketones and Mechanistic Investigation of the Organoindium
Reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
