$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Homoallylic Alcohols. 1-(2,4-Dinitrophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (15a). A mixture
of 2,4-dinitrobenzaldehyde (9.6 mg, 0.049 mmol), fluorous allytin 6b
(92.4 mg, 0.073 mmol), 13a (7.0 mg, 0.0025 mmol), and BTF (2.5 mL) was
stirred at 60 °C for 24 h. After removal of the solvent, the residue was
loaded onto a short column packed with fluorous reverse-phase silica gel
(1.0 g). The column was eluted with acetonitrile (3 mL).
1-(3-Bromophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (15h): 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.28-2.58
(m, 3H), 4.72 (dd, J = 7.8, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 5.12-5.22 (m, 2H), 5.73-5.84 (m,
1H), 7.19-7.54 (m, 4H); EIMS m/z 185/187 (M - C3H5)+, 157/159, 128, 105,
77.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM BTF (sic) solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Separation of "Light Fluorous" Reagents and Catalysts by Fluorous
Solid-Phase Extraction: Synthesis and Study of a Family of
Triarylphosphines Bearing Linear and Branched Fluorous Tags
