$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol (8). To a solution of 5-methylfurfural 12 (550 mg, 5.1 mmol) in
THF (10 mL) at −15 °C was added allyl magnesium bromide (1.0 M in THF,
6.5 mL, 6.5 mmol) dropwise over 10 min. The reaction mixture was stirred
for an additional 20 min and then quenched with water (10 mL). The
aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x10 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated. The residue
was purified via silica gel chromatography (10:1 to 8:1 hexane/ethyl
acetate) to afford racemic 13. Light yellow oil, yield (700 mg, 92%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
