$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure B (via aldehyde 2a): The mixture was
concentrated in vacuo and purified by General Procedure B for the
Preparation of Adducts 3a-3c from Furfurals 2a-2c: To a flame dried
re-sealable reaction tube purged with argon and containing a magnetic
stirrer, was added [Ir(cod)Cl]2 (6.7 mg, 0.010 mmol, 2.5 mol%),
(R)-Cl,MeO-BIPHEP (13.0 mg, 0.020 mmol, 5 mol%), 3-nitro-4-chlorobenzoic
acid (8.1 mg, 0.040 mmol 10 mol%), Cs2CO3 (26.1 mg, 0.080 mmol, 20 mol%)
and the furfural (0.40 mmol, 100 mol%). THF (2.0 mL, 0.2 M concentration
with respect to the furfural), i-PrOH (61 μL, 0.80 mmol, 200 mol%) and
allyl acetate (86 μL, 0.80 mmol, 200 mol%) were added and the reaction
mixture was allowed to stir at 100 °C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture
was concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash column chromatography
(SiO2) to furnish the corresponding products of allylation 3a-3c.
Procedure B (via aldehyde 2b): The reaction mixture was concentrated in
vacuo and purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2: pentane:Et2O,
5:1) to furnish the title compound (56.2 mg, 92% yield, 94% ee) as a
colorless oil. (R)-1-(5-methylfuran-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol (3b). TLC (SiO2):
Rf (Hexane:Et2O, 10:1) = 0.07. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 6.09 (d, J = 3.1
Hz, 1H), 5.87 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 1H), 5.79 (dddd, J = 17.2, 10.2, 7.2, 6.9
Hz, 1H), 5.12 (m, 2H), 4.65 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 2.58 (m, 2H), 2.25 (s,
3H), 2.10 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 154.3, 151.9, 134.2, 118.5,
107.1, 106.2, 67.1, 40.2, 13.7. HRMS (CI): Calcd. for C9H11O2 (M-H)+:
151.0759, Found: 151.0756. FTIR (neat): 3392, 3078, 2922, 1663, 1513,
1219, 914, 783 cm-1. Opt. Rot. [α]D26 = -30.0 (c = 0.81, in CH2Cl2) for
95% ee (R)-3b, Lit.5 [α]D26 = -24.8 (c = 0.98, CH2Cl2) for 94% ee (R)-3b.
HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H column, Hexane:i-PrOH, 98:2, 0.5 mL/min, 210 nm):
tmajor= 17.2 min, tminor= 18.2 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
