$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of allylic alcohols. Procedure A. 330
mg (1.25 mmol) of (1-bromovinyl)triisopropylsilane (S3) was put into a
flame-dried argon-filled 25 mL flask (Note: compound (S3) is a mixture of
the liquid and crystals at room temperature; for the use in reactions it
was molten in a 60 °C water bath and weighed in the liquid form). 6 mL of
THF was added and the solution was cooled to -78 °C. 0.78 mL (1.25 mmol)
of 1.6M solution of BuLi in hexanes was then added dropwise. The mixture
was left at -78 °C for 1 h. The aldehyde (1 mmol) was then slowly added.
After an additional hour, the reaction was quickly allowed to room
temperature and poured into water. The product was extracted with
dichloromethane; the combined extracts were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4
and concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel in 1:10 ethyl acetate - hexanes.
1-Phenyl-2-(triethylsilyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (1c) Prepared by Procedure A
from (S6) and benzaldehyde (259 mg, 2.44 mmol) as a pale yellowish liquid
(604 mg, 76%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33-7.24 (m, 5H), 6.01 (t, J =
1.9 Hz, 1H), 5.54-5.52 (m, 1H), 5.31-5.29 (m, 1H), 1.90 (d, J = 3.8 Hz,
1H), 0.82 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 9H), 0.53-0.39 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 150.6, 142.4, 128.2, 127.6, 127.3, 127.1, 125.3, 77.6, 7.1, 3.0;
For [MNa]+ C15H24NaOSi calculated 271.1494, found (TOF MS ES+) 271.1494;
FTIR (film, NaCl) νmax 3395 (m), 3062 (w), 3029 (w), 2953 (s), 2910 (m),
2875 (s), 1493 (w), 1455 (m), 1417 (m), 1378 (w), 1237 (m), 1192 (w),
1170 cm-1 (w).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
