$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: IV. General Procedure for the Allylation and
Crotylation of Aldehydes and Ketones with Acid Allyldioxazaborolidine 1
(0.17-0.31 g, 1.1-2.0 mmol) was dissolved in 2.0-3.0 mL of dry CH2Cl2
(0.5 M with respect to 1) and stirred at 25 °C for 10 min. The aldehyde
or ketone (1.0 mmol) was added by syringe dropwise over 1 min. If the
aldehyde or ketone was a solid, it was added with allyldioxazaborolidine
before dissolving both in CH2Cl2. The reaction flask was charged with
acid (1.1-2.0 mmol) by microliter syringe dropwise over 30 s. The
reaction was stirred at 25 °C and monitored by TLC until the aldehyde or
ketone had been completely consumed or overnight with no monitoring.
After completion, the reaction was diluted with 3 mL of CH2Cl2, quenched
with 3.0 mL of 1.0 M HCl or H2O if the substrate is acid sensitive. The
mixture was washed with 5 mL of saturated NaHCO3 solution and 5 mL of
brine, dried with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to yield the
homoallylic alcohol. Further purification by flash chromatography
(hexanes/ethyl acetate on silica gel) was performed if needed.
1-(3-Methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (6). Yield 95% 1H NMR (500MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.23 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.91 (m, 2H), 6.80 (d, J = 8.5, 1H), 5.77-5.82
(tdd, J = 7.0, 7.0, 16.5 Hz, 1H), 5.11-5.17 (m, 2H), 4.68 (m, 1H), 3.79
(s, 3H), 2.48 (m, 2H), 2.21 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.7,
145.8, 134.6, 129.5, 118.3, 118.2, 113.0, 111.4, 73.4, 55.2, 43.8.7 IR
(thin film) 3400 (br), 3075, 3002, 2937, 2837 cm-1; HRMS (ES/MeOH) m / z
calcd for C11H14NaO2 (M + Na)+ 201.0892, found 201.0890. Spectral data
were consistent with those previously reported in the literature.8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
