$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol 12. To a solution of 1-hexyne (37 mg, 0.45 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in
THF (1 mL) at -78 ºC was added a solution of n-BuLi (2.5 M in hexane,
0.19 mL, 0.48 mmol, 1.6 equiv) dropwise. After the resulting solution was
stirred for 45 min at -78 ºC, a solution of aldehyde 4 (43 mg, 0.30 mmol,
1.0 equiv) in THF (1.5 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was warmed to
-60 ºC over 40 min and then cooled to -78 ºC. A solution of benzaldehyde
(61 mg, 0.90 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in THF/HMPA (1.0/0.21 mL) was added, and
the resulting reaction mixture was warmed to ambient temperature. After
stirring for 30 min, 1M H2SO4 (1mL) and then water (4 mL) were added. The
mixture was stirred for 10 min at ambient temperature and then extracted
with ether (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with a
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) and brine (5 mL), dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. Flash chromatography on
silica gel, using ethyl acetate-hexanes (1:2) as eluant, provided a 1:1
diastereomeric mixture of alcohol 12 (64 mg, 0.25 mmol, 83% yield)
colorless oil. For both diastereomers (1:1 mixture): Rf 0.50
(hexanes/ethyl acetate 2/1); IR (film) 3314 (br s), 3086 (m), 3063 (m),
3030 (m), 2957 (s), 2872 (m), 2281 (w), 2225 (w), 1647 (w), 1604 (w),
1453 (s), 1054 (s), 700 (s) cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 1:1 mixture)δ
7.40-7.31 (m, 8H), 7.30-7.24 (m, 2H), 5.38 (s, 1H), 5.31 (s, 1H), 4.81
(dd, J = 9.9 and 3.1 Hz, 1H), 2.78 (dd, J = 14.5 and 3.3 Hz, 1H), 2.72
(dd, J = 14.4, and 9.9 Hz, 1H), 2.56 (dd, J = 14.5 and 2.8 Hz, 1H), 2.49
(dd, J = 14.5 and 9.1 Hz, 1H), 2.27-2.21 (m, 4H), 1.53-1.46 (m, 4H),
1.45-1.38 (m, 4H), 0.91 (app t, J = 7.2 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,CDCl3,
1:1 mixture) δ 145.6, 144.6, 144.2, 143.9, 128.5, 128.4, 128.3, 127.5,
127.3, 126.9, 125.7, 116.6, 116.2, 87.4, 87.1, 79.4, 79.1, 74.3, 73.1,
66.1, 66.0, 65.1, 42.9, 42.4, 30.61, 30.58, 21.94, 21.91, 18.4, 13.5 ;
high resolution mass spectrum (CI) m/z 240.1524 [(M-H2O)+; calcd for
C17H20O: 240.1514].
