$DATUM Preparation of 1-(3-Methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1c)4 Following the
Representative Procedure, 3-methoxybenzaldehyde (136 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexane/MTBE (10:1, 100 mL, 4:1, 100 mL)
provided 1c (148 mg, 83%) as a colorless oil.
1-(3-Methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1c)4, yield 148 mg, 83%. Data for 1c:
1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.29-7.26 (m, 1 H, Aryl), 6.95-6.93 (m, 2 H,
Aryl), 6.84-6.80 (m, 1 H, Ar), 5.81 (ddt, J = 17.1, 10.2, 7.1, 1 H,
HC(3)), 5.20-5.15 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 4.73 (ddd, J = 7.8, 4.8, 2.2, 1 H,
HC(1), 3.82 (s, 3 H, H3C(7')), 2.57-2.44 (m, 2 H), 2.13 (d, J = 2.2, 1 H,
OH) 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 159.7 (C(3')), 145.6 (C(1')), 134.4 (C(3)),
129.4 (C(5')), 118.4 (C(6')), 118.1 (C(4)), 113.0 (C(4')), 111.3 (C(2')),
73.2 (C(1)), 55.2 (C(7')) , 43.7 (C(2))IR: (NaCl) 34.19 (m), 3075 (m),
3004 (m), 2937 (m), 2835 (m), 1601 (s), 1585 (s), 1489 (s), 1455 (s),
1435 (s), 1315 (m), 1287 (s), 1264 (s), 1155 (m) HRMS: (EI, 70 eV) Calcd.
for C11H14O2, 178.0993; found, 178.0986 TLC: Rf 0.27 (hexanes/MTBE, 4:1)
[UV, CAM]
