$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for preparation of
anti-β-hydroxyallylsilanes 8a-f: ( d Ipc)2BH (143 mg, 0.50 mmol) was
weighed into a round-bottom flask containing a stir bar in a glove box.
(Note: The crystalline borane should be crushed and pulverized to fine
powder with a glass rod in order to ensure efficient hydroboration). The
flask was capped with a rubber septum and removed from the glove box and
placed in a cold bath at -40 °C. Toluene (2.5 mL) was added to the flask
and the mixture (suspension) was stirred at -40 °C for 10 min.
Allenylsilane 5 (96 mg, 0.55 mmol) was added neat via a microliter
syringe. This mixture was slowly warmed up to 0 °C and stirred for
additional 5 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C and a freshly
distilled aldehyde (0.45 mmol) was added at -78 °C dropwise to the
reaction mixture via microliter syringe. The mixture was stirred for 12 h
at -78 °C. MeOH (0.1 mL) was added at -78 °C and the reaction was allowed
to warm to 0 °C. To the 0 °C mixture was added saturated NaHCO3 (0.5 mL)
followed by slow addition of 30% H2O2 (1.0 mL). The reaction was stirred
vigorously for ~5 h at room temperature. Brine (2 mL) was added, the
organic layer was separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O
(3 x 3 mL). The combined organic extracts were dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Purification of the crude product was by flash chromatography (gradient
elution: hexane:Et2O = 100:1 to 10:1). Homoallylic alcohols 8a-f as
colorless oils. (1R,2S)-2-(dimethyl(phenyl)silyl)-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol
(8c). 5, 7, 8 A colorless oil; 83% yield, 84% ee; [α]D 25 .8 = -12.2° (c
1.13, CHCl3), 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.47-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.36-7.30 (m,
3H), 7.29-7.20 (m, 5H), 5.88 (dt, J = 17.2, 10.4, 1H), 5.05 (dd, J =
10.4, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 4.90 (dd, J = 17.2, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 4.75 (dd, J = 7.2,
2.4 Hz, 1H), 2.26 (dd, J =10.4, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 2.04 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H),
0.19 (s, 3H), 0.08 (s, 3H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.0, 137.7,
136.0, 134.4, 129.4, 128.5, 128.0, 127.94, 127.0, 116.5, 74.5, 45.3,
-3.1, -3.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective syntheses of syn- and anti-β-hydroxyallylsilanes via
allene hydroboration-aldehyde allylboration reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Ming; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(8), 1992-1995

