$DATUM Synthesis of 1-(2-(hydroxymethyl)phenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (13): To a
solution of o-bromobenzyl alcohol (935 mg, 5 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was
added n-butyl lithium (20 mmol, 8 mL) at -78 °C. The mixture was stirred
at this temperature for 1 h, and then at 0 °C for 2 h. The acrolein (20
mmol, 1.66 mL) was added to the reaction mixture via the syringe through
a septum cap under N2. After 4 hours, the reaction was quenched by
addition of a saturated solution of NH4Cl (5 mL), and extracted with
ether (3 × 15 mL). The combined organic phase was dried over Na2SO4, the
solvent was removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by a flash
chromatography on silica gel to give compound 13 in 70% (575 mg);. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.28-7.19 (m, 4H), 6.00 (ddd, J = 17.0, 10.6, 5.2 Hz,
1H), 5.28-5.25 (m, 2H), 5.16 (d, J = 10.6 Hz, 1H), 4.52 (s, 2H), 4.24
(brs, 1H), 3.95 (brs, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 140.8, 139.0,
138.4, 129.8, 128.3, 128.0, 127.7, 115.0, 72.6, 63.2; LRMS (EI): 164
(M+).
