$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(Furan-2-yl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol (22) A solution of furfuraldehyde
(976 mg, 10.17 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was cooled to -78 °C and the reaction
mixture was treated with a 0.5M solution of 1-methyl-2-propenylmagnesium
bromide (25 mL, 12.25 mmol) in THF. The reaction mixture was left to
warm-up to room temperature and stirred for further 2 hours. The reaction
mixture was diluted with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (50 mL) and the aqueous
layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL). The organic extracts were
combined and extracted with brine (20 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by FCC (petrol-EtOAc 19:1 to 9:1)
afforded the homoallylic alcohol 22 (1.52g, 98%, 1:1 dr) as a clear oil.
1-(Furan-2-yl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol (22), yield (1.52g, 98%, 1:1 dr). 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) 7.37 (2H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 6.33 (2H, br. s.), 6.27
(1H, d, J = 3.0 Hz), 6.23 (1H, d, J = 3.0 Hz), 5.89-5.66 (2H, m),
5.28-4.99 (4H, m), 4.56 (1H, t, J = 6.0 Hz), 4.42 (1H, dd, J = 4.0, 7.5
Hz), 2.81-2.57 (2H, m), 2.22 (1H, d, J = 4.0 Hz), 2.17 (1H, d, J = 6.0
Hz), 1.07 (3H, d, J = 7.0 Hz), 0.95 (3H, d, J = 7.0 Hz). 13C NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) 155.3, 155.0, 141.9, 141.6, 139.9, 139.6, 116.9, 115.8, 110.0 (two
signals), 107.2, 106.8, 71.3, 43.5, 43.0, 16.2, 15.0 (only 17 signals
were observed).
