$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.1. Synthesis of (±)-(4R,2E,5Z)-5-(p-tolylsulfenyl)deca-2,5-dien-4-ol,
(±)-22h. To a solution of vinyl sulfide 211 (1.012 g, 2.203 mmol) in 11
mL of THF, cooled to -78 °C was added 1.2 equiv of n-BuLi (1.65 mL) and
was stirred at this temperature. After 10 min 2.0 equiv of freshly
distilled crotonaldehyde (0.365 mL, 0.309 g, 4.41 mmol) was added
dropwise and the resulting colorless solution was stirred at this
temperature for 10 min. The reaction mixture was quenched with a
saturated solution of NH4Cl (2 mL/mmol) and H2O (2 mL/mmol), diluted with
EtOAc (3 mL/mmol) and the layers were separated. The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (3 times, 4 mL/mmol). The combined organic extracts
were washed with a saturated solution of NaCl (4 mL/mmol), dried over
MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to give crude hydroxy vinyl
sulfide (±)-22h. Chromatographic purification (5-40% Et2O-hexane) gave
(±)-22h as a oil. Colorless oil, yield (0.590 g, 96%). Rf 0.25 (20%
Et2O-hexane). 1H NMR (400 MHz), COSY δ 0.87 (t, 3 H, J = 7.1 Hz, H-10),
1.25-1.39 (m, 4 H, H-8, H-9), 1.66 (dq, 1 H, J = 6.4, 0.8 Hz, H-1), 2.17
(d, 1 H, J = 5.1 Hz, OH), 2.28 (s, 3 H, CH3 p-Tol), 2.31-2.37 (m, 2 H,
H-7), 4.50 (td, 1 H, J = 6.0, 0.8 Hz, H-4), 5.49 (ddq, 1 H, J = 15.2,
6.5, 1.4 Hz, H-3), 5.66 (dqd, 1 H, J = 15.3, 6.5, 1.0 Hz, H-2), 6.27 (td,
1 H, J = 7.2, 0.9 Hz, H-6), 7.05 (d, 2 H, J = 8.5 Hz, p-Tol), 7.16 (d, 2
H, J = 8.2 Hz, p-Tol). 13C NMR (100 MHz), HSQC δ 13.9 (C-10), 17.7 (C-1),
20.9 (CH3 p-Tol), 22.3 (C-9), 29.4 (C-7), 31.1 (C-8), 75.3 (C-4), 127.9
(C-2), 128.7 (2 x p-Tol), 129.6 (2 x p-Tol), 131.7 (C-3), 131.9 and 135.1
and 135.7 (C-5 and 2 x p-Tol), 138.5 (C-6). IR (film): 3401, 3072, 3020,
2958, 2925, 2872, 2858, 1670, 1630, 1598, 1492, 1451, 1399, 1378, 1118,
1086, 1017, 963, 806 cm-1. HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C17H25OS [M+H]+
277.1626, found 277.1449.
