$DATUM (E)-1-(2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)phenyl)hex-5-en-1-ol (11g).
5-Bromo-1-pentene (1.86 g, 12.5 mmol) was added so slowly to a mixture of
Mg (316 mg, 13 mmol) in THF (20 ml) that the mixture was kept mild
refluxing. After addition, the mixture was stirred for 2 h. To a solution
of (E)-2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)benzaldehyde (10a) (780 mg, 4.8 mmol) in
THF (20 ml) was added a solution of above Grignard reagent (12.5 mmol) at
room temperature. The reaction solution was stirred for 10 h under
refluxing. After the reaction was cooled to 0 °C, an aqueous saturated
solution of NH4Cl (30 ml) was added dropwise and the resulting mixture
was stirred for 10 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with diethyl
ether (30 mL × 3). The combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuum. The crude residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 1/1). Product 11g
as yellowish oil (939 mg, 84% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
1.31-1.39 (m, 1H), 1.44-1.53 (m, 1H), 1.68-1.75 (m, 2H), 2.00-2.06 (m,
2H), 2.98 (br, 2H), 4.20 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H), 4.89-4.99 (m, 3H),
5.70-5.80 (m, 1H), 6.08 (dt, J = 15.6, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (d, J = 16 Hz,
1H), 7.18-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.36-7.41 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
25.0, 33.4, 37.2, 63.2, 70.5, 114.6, 125.7, 126.5, 127.3, 127.6, 127.7,
131.0, 134.8, 138.5, 141.5; MS (EI) m/z (rel) 145 (48), 131 (14), 129
(17), 118 (12), 117 (100), 116 (11), 115 (46), 91 (21); HRMS for C15H18O
[M-H2O]+: 214.1358; Found: 214.1353; IR (film): 3349 (br), 2929 (m), 2858
(s), 1214 (m), 995 (s), 967 (s), 912 (s), 757 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM crude from stage 1 added in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of 2,3-Disubstituted Indanones via
Pd-Catalyzed Intramolecular Asymmetric Allylic Alkylation of Ketones
