$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Reformatsky reaction:
synthesis of β-hydroxy esters (13b-13h) (13a is commercially available)
TMSCl (1.2 equiv) was added to a suspension of Zn dust (1.6 equiv) in
Et2O (0.4 M solution) at rt. The resulting mixture was stirred for 15 min
and then heated to reflux whilst a mixture of aldehyde (1.0 equiv) and
ethyl bromoacetate (1.2 equiv) was added at such a rate so as to maintain
a gentle reflux (~ 20 min). The reaction mixture was heated at reflux for
1 h and then allowed to cool to rt before quenching carefully with
hydrochloric acid (2 M, 1 × volume of organic phase). The layers were
separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × volumes of
aqueous phase). The combined organic extracts were washed with H2O (1/6 ×
volume of organic phase), brine (1/6 × volume of organic phase) and then
dried (MgSO4). The volatiles were removed under reduced pressure and the
resulting β -hydroxy ester used directly without further purification.
(E)-Ethyl 3-hydroxy-5-phenyl-pent-4-enoate (13g) See general
experimental: a mixture of trans-cinnamaldehyde (3.00 mL, 24.00 mmol) and
ethyl bromoacetate (3.20 mL, 29.00 mmol) was added to a suspension of Zn
dust (2.500 g, 38.00 mmol, activated with TMSCl (3.60 mL, 29.00 mmol)) in
Et2O (60 mL). Aqueous work-up afforded alcohol 13g as a yellow oil (4.290
g, 81%, purity 85% by 1H NMR), which was used without further
purification in the following step: Data were consistent with those
reported in the literature.8 Rf = 0.26 (20% EtOAc in hexane);
νmax(film)/cm-13444s br (OH), 3081w, 3058w, 3025m, 2981s, 2936s, 2901m,
1948w, 1881w, 1730vs (C=O), 1599m (C=C), 1577m, 1494m, 1448s, 1397s,
1371s, 1255s, 1162s, 1099s, 1070s, 1033s, 967s, 876m, 852m, 802w, 752s,
694s; δH (300 MHz) 1.27 (t, J 7.1, 3H, OCH2CH3), 2.55-2.71 (stack, 2H,
CH2CO2Et), 4.18 (q, J 7.1, 2H, OCH2CH3), 4.72 (app. q, J 5.9, 1H, CHOH),
6.22 (dd, J 15.8, 6.2, 1H, PhCH=CH), 6.65 (d, J 15.8, 1H, PhCH=CH),
7.18-7.41 (stack, 5H, PhH), OH not observed; δC(75 MHz) 14.2 (CH3,
OCH2CH3), 41.5 (CH2, C-2), 60.8 (CH2, OCH2CH3), 68.8 (CH, CHOH), 126.5
(CH), 127.8 (CH), 128.6 (CH), 130.0 (CH), 130.7 (CH), 136.4 (quat. C,
ipsoPh), 172.2 (quat. C, C=O); m/z (EI) 220 ([M]+, 6%), 202 (11,
[M-H2O]+), 131 (100), 103 (61), 77 (51, [C6H5]+), 51 (39).
