$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1S,2S)-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol An oven-dried sealed
tube under an atmosphere of N2 was charged with 4-methoxybenzaldehyde 3b
(27.2 mg, 0.20 mmol, 100 mol%), (S)-I (10.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 5 mol%), K3PO4
(21.5 mg, 0.10 mmol, 50 mol%), THF (0.1 mL, 2.0 M), isopropanol (31 μL,
0.4 mmol, 200 mol%), and H2O (18 μL, 1.0 mmol, 500 mol%). But-3-en-2-yl
acetate 1 (45.6 mg, 0.40 mmol, 200 mol%) was added and the mixture was
allowed to stir at ambient temperature for 0.5 hr, at which point the
reaction vessel was placed in an oil bath at 60°C and was allowed to stir
for 48 hr. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. Purification
of the residue by column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl acetate: hexanes,
1:20 with 0.1% TEA) provided 4b (34.2 mg, 0.178 mmol) as a colorless oil
in 89% yield (12:1 dr). HPLC: (Chiralpak AD-H/AD-H column, hexanes:i-PrOH
= 95:5, 0.5 mL/min, 230 nm), tminor = 40.2 min, tmajor = 47.6 min; ee =
98%.
