$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Detailed Procedure and Spectral Data for anti-Diastereo-and
Enantioselective Carbonyl Crotylation from the Aldehyde Oxidation Level
(1S,2S)-1-(4-bromophenyl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol An oven-dried sealed tube
under an atmosphere of N2 was charged with 4-bromobenzaldehyde 3a (37.0
mg, 0.20 mmol, 100 mol%), (S)-I (10.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 5 mol%), K3PO4 (21.5
mg, 0.10 mmol, 50 mol%), THF (0.1 mL, 2.0 M), isopropanol (31 μL, 0.4
mmol, 200 mol%), and H2O (18 μL, 1.0 mmol, 500 mol%). But-3-en-2-yl
acetate 1 (45.6 mg, 0.40 mmol, 200 mol%) was added and the mixture was
allowed to stir at ambient temperature for 0.5 hr, at which point the
reaction vessel was placed in an oil bath at 60°C and was allowed to stir
for 48 hr. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. Purification
of the residue by column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl acetate: hexanes,
1:20 with 0.1% TEA) provided 4a (39.5 mg, 0.164 mmol) as a colorless oil
in 82% yield (17:1 dr). HPLC: (Chiralpak AS-H/AS-H column, hexanes:i-PrOH
= 98:2, 0.5 mL/min, 230 nm), tminor = 27.9 min, tmajor = 31.8 min; ee =
98%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, oven-dried sealed tube; sixth stage pre-heated oil bath
(17:1 d.r., 98% e.e.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
