$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Hydroxyallylation Reactions Using Indium in
THF. Typical Procedure (A). 3-Bromopropenyl acetate 5 (0.175 mL, 1.5
mmol) was added at 0 °C to a suspension of indium powder (0.115 g, 1
mmol) in THF (2 mL). The heterogeneous mixture was stirred for 30 min at
0 °C, the ice bath was removed, and stirring was continued for 3.5 h at
rt. Benzaldehyde (0.105 mL, 1 mmol) was added at 0 °C, and the reaction
mixture was stirred for 4 h at 0 °C. Synthesis of
1-phenylbut-3-ene-1,2-diol (2a). Typical Procedure. The crude reaction
mixture obtained by procedure A or B was dissolved in MeOH/H2O (5 mL, 9:1
v/v), K2CO3 (0.415 g, 3 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture was
stirred at rt overnight. MeOH was removed at reduced pressure, and the
aqueous layer was extracted with ether. The combined organic layers were
dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated at reduce pressure. Purification by flash
chromatography on SiO2 (cyclohexane/ethyl acetate 8:2) afforded 0.105 g
of syn-2a (0.64 mmol, 64%) and 0.035 g of anti-2a (0.21 mmol, 21%).
syn-1-(2-Furyl)but-3-ene-1,2-diol
(syn-2g).anti-1-(2-Furyl)but-3-ene-1,2-diol (anti-2g). 1H NMR (200 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 2.54 (s, 1H), 2.75 (s, 1H), 4.43-4.51 (m, 1H), 4.56 (dd, J =
5.0/7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (dt, J = 1.8/10.5 Hz, 1H), 5.35 (dt, J = 1.8/17.2
Hz, 1H), 5.80 (ddd, J = 5.2/10.5/17.2 Hz, 1H), 6.33-6.39 (m, 2H),
7.40-7.43 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 70.9, 74.5, 108.0, 110.1,
117.1, 135.8, 142.1, 153.0. Anal. Calcd for C8H10O3: C, 62.33; H, 6.54.
Found: C, 62.39; H, 6.47. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.40-4.46 (m, 1H),
4.75 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 5.23 (dt, J = 1.4/10.5 Hz, 1H), 5.39 (dt, J =
1.4/17.2 Hz, 1H), 5.87 (ddd, J = 5.6/10.5/17.2 Hz, 1H), 6.32-6.39 (m,
2H), 7.40-7.42 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 70.7, 74.7, 107.7,
110.1, 117.4, 135.6, 117.4, 135.6, 141.9, 153.0. Anal. Calcd for C8H10O3:
C, 62.33; H, 6.54. Found: C, 62.36; H, 6.59.
