$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetic acid
9-(tert-butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxy)-2,4,6,8-tetramethyl-11-trimethylsilanyl-undeca-2,4,6,10-tetraenyl
ester, 12. To a flame dried flask purged with Ar was added 2-bromopropene
(0.1 mL, 1.18 mmol) dissolved in THF (5 mL). The flask was cooled to -78
°C and t-BuLi (1.5 M in pentane, 1.57 mL, 2.36 mmol) was added slowly by
syringe. The mixture was allowed to stir for 20 minutes. Aldehyde 10 (225
mg, 0.59 mmol) in THF (1.5 mL) dried over molecular sieves was slowly
added to the vinyl lithium reagent by syringe. The reaction was quenched
with NH4Cl (aq) (2 mL) at -78 °C after 25 minutes. The mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature. The layers were separated and the
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 x 10 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated to yield a
crude oil. The mixture was purified via column chromatography to yield
alcohol 11 (197 mg, 0.47 mmol, 80%) as a mixture of diastereomers. The
diastereomers were not separated (A 1H NMR spectrum of the mixture is
provided). 11, yield (80%, 197 mg, 0.47 mmol)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
