$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-4,4-Difluoro-1-phenylhexa-1,5-dien-3-ol (2). To a suspension of
cinnamaldehyde (2.74 g, 20.7 mmol) and indium powder(3.57 g, 31.1 mmol)
in H2O (200 mL) was added 3-bromo-3,3- difluoropropene (4.88 g, 31.1
mmol) at room temperature. After stirring for 16 h, the reaction mixture
was quenched with 1 M HCl aqueous solution (20 mL) and was extracted with
Et2O. The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether: ethyl acetate = 5:1)
to afford 2 (3.29 g, 76% yield) as a yellow oil 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)δ
7.25-7.42 (m, 5H), 6.76 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 6.19 (dd, J = 16.1, 6.5 Hz,
1H), 6.00 (ddd, J = 23.1, 17.4, 11.1 Hz, 1H), 5.70-5.78 (m, 1H), 5.55 (d,
J = 11.1 Hz, 1H), 4.45-4.55 (m, 1H), 2.28 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H); 19F NMR
(282 MHz, CDCl3) δ-108.7 (dt, J = 248.0, 10.1 Hz, 1F), -110.7 (dt,J =
249.3, 10.3 Hz, 1F).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
