$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for asymmetric ethylation
(Table. 2): To a solution of chiral Schiff base (0.018 mmol) in solvent
(4 mL) at -40 °C was added diethylzinc (0.37mL, 3.6 mmol). The solution
was warmed up to 0 °C, stirred for 30 min and then cooled to -40 °C
again, when aldehyde (1.8 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for 24
h at 0 °C and was then quenched by 1N HCl aq. (20 mL). After extraction
with diethylether (20 mL x 3), silica-gel column chromatography [eluent,
hexane-ethyl acetate (10:1)] and Kugelrohr distillation, a product was
obtained. The ee was determined by HPLC analysis using chiral column.
1-Furyl-1-propanol: [α]D26 = +25.9 (c 2.10, CHCl3) (lit.2 [α]D20 = +14.3
(c 2.20, CHCl3, 78% ee (R))). The ee of the product was determined as 90%
ee by HPLC analysis of its benzoate. : tR of R -isomer, 11.07 min; tR of
S-isomer, 12.60 min [column, CHIRALCEL AD-H (DAICEL): eluent,
hexane-2-propanol (98:2), 0.5 mL/min].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New Chiral Schiff Base as a Tridentate Ligand for Catalytic
Enantioselective Addition of Diethylzinc to Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tanaka, Takanori; Yasuda, Yorinobu; Hayashi, Masahiko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(18), 7091-7093

