$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of allylic
alcohols. Procedure A. 330 mg (1.25 mmol) of
(1-bromovinyl)triisopropylsilane (S3) was put into a flame-dried
argon-filled 25 mL flask (Note: compound (S3) is a mixture of the liquid
and crystals at room temperature; for the use in reactions it was molten
in a 60 °C water bath and weighed in the liquid form). 6 mL of THF was
added and the solution was cooled to -78 °C. 0.78 mL (1.25 mmol) of 1.6M
solution of BuLi in hexanes was then added dropwise. The mixture was left
at -78 °C for 1 h. The aldehyde (1 mmol) was then slowly added. After an
additional hour, the reaction was quickly allowed to room temperature and
poured into water. The product was extracted with dichloromethane; the
combined extracts were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated. The
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel in 1:10 ethyl
acetate - hexanes.
(E)-2-Methyl-1-phenyl-4-(triisopropylsilyl)penta-1,4-dien-3-ol (1r)
Prepared by Procedure A from (E)-α -methylcinnamaldehyde (469 mg, 3.2
mmol); purified in 1:25 ethyl acetate - hexanes system to give the
product as a colorless oil (928 mg, 89%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.36-7.20 (m, 5H), 6.62 (s, 1H), 6.19-6.17 (m, 1H), 5.63 (d, J = 1.7 Hz,
1H), 4.90 (d, J = 3.3 Hz, 1H), 1.82 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 3H), 1.60 (d, J = 4.0
Hz, 1H), 1.25 (sep, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.11 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 9H), 1.07 (d, J
= 7.4 Hz, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 147.5, 138.7, 137.6, 128.9,
128.4, 128.0, 127.6, 126.4, 79.3, 18.7, 18.7, 13.9, 11.3; For [MNa]+
C21H34NaOSi calculated 353.2277, found (TOF MS ES+) 353.2286; FTIR (film,
NaCl) νmax 3440 (m), 3057 (m), 3024 (m), 2944 (s), 2890 (s), 2865 (s),
1600 (w), 1492 (m), 1464 (s), 1383 (s), 1366 cm-1 (s).
