$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedures for the Preparation of 1,4-Octadien-7-yn-3-ols 14
4-Methyl-5,8-diphenyl-1,4-octadien-7-yn-3-ol (14); To a solution of
enynal (0.61 mmol) in THF (0.5 mL) was added vinylmagnesium chloride (1.5
M solution in THF, 0.73 mmol) at -78 °C. The mixture was stirred for 20
min at the same temperature and then quenched by addition of water. After
extraction three times with EtOAc, the combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 3/1)
(81% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.57 (s, 3H), 1.93 (br s, 1H), 3.46 (d, J =
17.6 Hz, 1H), 3.55 (d, J = 17.9 Hz, 1H), 5.24 (dt, J = 10.5, 1.2 Hz, 1H),
5.40-5.47 (m, 2H), 5.85 (ddd, J = 17.8, 10.8, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 7.24-7.28 (m,
6H), 7.31-7.37 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.10, 24.45, 71.92, 81.61,
87.75, 114.90, 123.64, 126.72, 127.67, 128.13, 128.15, 128.41, 131.44,
132.83, 134.35, 138.24, 142.53; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C21H20OK (M++K),
327.1151 found 327.1154.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Styrenes Using Ruthenium-Catalyzed Ring-Closing Enyne
Metathesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
