$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of bromobenzene (3.96 g, 2.7 mL, 25.2 mmol) in THF (50 mL)
was added n-BuLi (10.0 mL, 25.2 mmol, 2.5 M solution in hexanes) at -78
°C. After stirring at the same temperature for 1 h, s-1a (4.88 g, 21.0
mmol in 50 mL of THF) was added. The resulting solution was warmed to
room temperature and stirred for 8 h. Then the mixture was quenched with
saturated ammonium chloride solution. The reaction mixture was extracted
with ether and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated,
and the residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel (petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate = 10:1). compound 1a (6.49 g, 99%) as brown oil. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 3.11 (s, 1H), 5.36 (s, 1H), 6.95 (s, 1H),
7.19-7.33 (m, 11H), 7.47 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.86 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 77.6, 87.1, 97.9, 122.9, 124.3, 126.5,
127.6, 128.10, 128.12, 128.2, 128.26, 128.32, 128.8, 131.3, 133.8, 135.8,
141.8. HRMS (EI) calcd for C23H18O: 310.1358, found 310.1357.
