$DATUM 1-(4-Bromo-phenyl)-pent-4-en-1-ol Magnesium turnings (1.09 g, 44.8 mmol)
was stirred overnight under a flow of argon at room temperature.
Following the addition of THF (22.5 mL) and 1,2- dibromoethane (5 drops),
4-bromo-1-butene (1.83 mL, 18.0 mmol) was added at such a rate as to
ensure the flask was hot to touch throughout addition (approx 50 °C).
Following stirring for 2 h at room temperature, stirring was stopped and
the grey supernatant transferred to a stirred solution of
4-bromobenzaldehyde (2.22 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (12 mL) at -78 °C over 5
min. The resultant solution was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C, then warmed to
room temperature and stirred for 12 h. Sat. aq. NH4Cl (10 mL) was added
and the aqueous phase washed with Et2O (3 × 20 mL), the combined organics
were dried (MgSO4) and then evaporated under reduced pressure.
Purification of the residue by column chromatography (petroleum
ether/Et2O 92:8) gave 1-(4-bromo-phenyl)-pent-4-en-1-ol as a colorless
oil (2.60 g, 90%). 1-(4-Bromo-phenyl)-pent-4-en-1-ol, yield (2.60 g,
90%). R f 0.22 (petroleum ether/Et2O 92:8); IR (film) 3347br.s (O-H),
3077m, 2937s, 1640m (C=C), 1593w, 1405s, 1070s and 1010s cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.47 (2H, dd, J 8, 3), 7.24-7.20 (2H, m), 5.88-5.78
(1H, m), 5.07-4.99 (2H, m), 4.69-4.64 (1H, m), 2.20-1.71 (5H, m); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 143.5 (C), 137.9 (CH), 131.5 (2 × CH), 127.6 (2 × CH),
121.2 (C), 115.2 (CH2), 73.3 (CH), 38.0 (CH2), 29.9 (CH2); MS CI m/z
(rel. int.) 243 (81BrM + H+, 10), 242 (20), 241 (79BrM + H+, 10), 240
(25), 143 (100), 128 (60); HRMS m/z calcd for C11H14OBr, 241.0228, found
241.0234.
