$DATUM 1-(4-Bromo-phenyl)-pent-4-en-1-ol Magnesium turnings (1.08 g, 0.045 mol)
were mixed with Et2O (20 mL) and 4-bromo butene (3.38 g, 0.025 mol) in
Et2O (10 mL) was slowly added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1 h and then heated to reflux for another 30 min. The
Grignard reagent was slowly added to a solution of 4-bromo benzaldehyde
(4.07 g, 0.022 mol) in Et2O (30 mL) and the reaction mixture was heated
to reflux for 2 h. Ice (10 g) was added and the resulting suspension was
dissolved with HCl (2 M). The organic layer was separated, washed with
aqueous NaHSO3, aqueous NaHCO3 and H2O, and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of
the solvent and FC (MTBE/pentane, 1:10) afforded the desired product
(4.53 g, 85 %). 1-(4-Bromo-phenyl)-pent-4-en-1-ol, yield (4.53 g, 85 %).
IR (neat): 3350s, 3077m, 2935s, 1903w, 1675m, 1641m, 1587m, 1486s, 1402m,
1298w, 1199m, 1068s, 1008s, 912s, 821s, 719m, 638m cm-1. 1H-NMR (300
MHz): δ = 7.48-7.45 (m, 2 H, aryl-H), 7.22-7.20 (m, 2 H, aryl-H), 5.82
(tdd, J1 =16.9 Hz, J2 =10.2 Hz, J3 = 6.6 Hz, 1 H, CH2=CH), 5.07-4.98 (m,
2 H, CH=CH2), 4.66 (dd, J1 = 7.6 Hz, J2 = 5.5 Hz, 1 H, HCO), 2.16- 2.08
(m, 2 H, CH2), 1.95 (br s, 1 H, OH), 1.90-1.71 (m, 2 H, CH2). 13C-NMR (75
MHz): δ = 143.6 (C), 137.9 (CH), 131.5 (CH), 127.6 (CH), 121.3 (C), 115.2
(CH2), 73.3 (CH), 38.1 (CH2), 29.9 (CH2). MS (ESI): m/z = 263 ([M+Na]+).
HRMS: m/z = [M+Na]+ Calcd for C11H13BrONa: 263.0047, Found: 263.0042.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isonitrile Trapping Reactions under Thermolysis of Alkoxyamines for the
Synthesis of Quinolines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
