$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General procedure for addition of
dimethylzinc to aldehydes: To a solution of 1a (100 mg , 0.07 mmol) in
dry hexane (10 mL) was added freshly distilled titanium tetraisopropoxide
(415µL, 1.40 mmol), and the mixture was stirred for 30 min at room
temperature. To this mixture, Me2Zn (3 mL of 1 M solution in hexane, 3
mmol) was added and the resulting mixture was stirred for additional 15
min. The mixture was cooled to -35 °C and an appropriate aldehyde (1.18
mmol) was added slowly. The mixture was kept stirring at this temperature
and checked by GLC. After the peak of the starting aldehyde disappeared,
the mixture was quenched with NH4Cl, then the whole mixture was filtered
through a sintered glass. The product was extracted with an appropriate
solvent and purified by flash column chromatography. The ee is checked by
chiral HPLC. Racemic α-methyl carbinols were prepared by the reaction of
methylmagnesium bromide with the corresponding aldehydes and used to
confirm the separation of the racemates by hplc. The absolute
configuration of each product was estimated by the sign of optical
rotation in literature (R)-1-(Furan-2-yl)ethanol (Entry 12, Table 1):E.e.
= 97%. Yield =98%, [α ]D +7.86 (c 0.9, CHCl3). Lit.9 (R)-
1-(furan-2-yl)ethanol [α ]D +15.5 (c 2.02, CHCl3), 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
7.38-7.35 (1H, m), 6.32 (1H, dd, J = 3.4, 1.9 Hz), 6.22 (1H, d, J= 16.1
Hz), 4.87 (1H, q, J= 6.3), 2.20 (1H, s, disappeared with D2O) , 1.54 (3H,
d, J = 6.3 Hz), 13C NMR (CDCl3)δ: 21.35, 63.65, 105.03, 111.04, 141.77,
157.39. MS m/z: 112 (M+). HRMS Calcd. for C6H8O2: 112.0524 (M+). Found:
112.0516. HPLC analysis: column OD-H, detector setting is 220 nm,
hexane-isopropanol (97.5:2.5) 0.3 mL/m, retention time 42.68 min (R), (S)
not observed
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
