$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure IV. Preparation of
(S)-1-(2'-Naphthyl)-3-buten-1-ol (3ab) In a 10-mL, three-necked round
bottom flask fitted with a nitrogen inlet adapter, septum and
thermocouple, was placed a solution of 25d (50 mg, 0.1 mmol, 0.05 equiv)
in 5.0 mL of dichloromethane and 1.0 mL of diisopropylethylamine was
added 2-naphthylaldehyde (312 mg, 2.0 mmol). The solution was stirred at
–78 °C for 10 min before allylic trichlorosilane (580 μL, 4.0 mmol, 2.0
equiv) was added slowly. The resulting mixture was stirred at that
temperature for 8 h whereupon the cold solution was poured into a mixture
of 10 mL of sat. aq. NaHCO3 and 10 ml of sat. aq. KF solution at 0 °C
with vigorous stirring. The mixture was stirred for 2 h at room
temperature and then it was filtered through Celite. The layers were then
separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 30 mL).
The combined organic extracts were dried over Mg2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The oily residue was purified by column chromatography
((SiO2) CH2Cl2/pentane, 3/1 followed by CH2Cl2) to afford 364 mg (92%) of
3ab 13 as a colorless oil. Data for (–)-3ab: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3)
7.85-7.80 (m, 4 H, HC(2'), HC(4'), HC(7'), HC(9')), 7.52-7.45 (m, 3 H,
HC(5'), HC(6') HC(10')), 5.80 (dddd, J = 18.0, 9.5, 7.5, 7.0, 1 H,
HC(3)), 5.20 (dq, J = 17.2, 1.5, 1 H, HbC(4)), 5.16 (dq, J = 10.3, 1.5, 1
H, HaC(4)), 4.92 (dd, J = 7.7, 4.9, 1 H, HC(1)), 2.66-2.54 (m, 2 H,
HC(2)), 2.16 (br, 1 H, OH) 13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 141.4 (C(1')), 134.5
(C(3)), 133.4 (C(3')), 133.1 (C(8')), 128.4 (C(10')), 127.9 (C(7')),
126.3 (C(4')), 126.0 (C(2')), 124.7 (C(5')), 124.2 (C(6')), 118.8 (C(4)),
73.5 (C(1)), 44.0 (C(2)) IR: (NaCl) 3376 (m), 3057(w), 3017 (w), 2978
(w), 2931 (w), 2905 (w), 1640 (m), 1602 (m), 1508 (m), 1433 (m), 1415
(m), 1366 (m), 1271 (m), 1125 (m), 1049 (s), 916 (s), 857 (s), 819 (s),
748 (s) Opt. Rot.: [α]D 24 −33.66 (c = 1.06, benzene) (Lit.13 (R)-3ab:
[α]D 24 +22.4 (c = 1.85, benzene)) TLC: R f 0.38 (CH2Cl2) [KMnO4] SFC:
(S)-3ab t R 4.3 min (93.4%); (R)-3ab, t R, 4.8 min (6.6%) (Chiralpak OD,
40 °C, 150 bar, 8% MeOH in CO2, 3.0 mL/min, 220 nm).
