$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 3-butyl-2-bydroxy-4-[(1,1-dimethylethyl)
dimethylsilyloxy]-3-pentenoate (5b). Vinyl iodide 4b (2.21 g, 6.00 mmol)
was dissolved in dry diethyl ether (15 mL) under an argon atmosphere. The
solution was cooled to -78 °C, tBuLi (7.50 mL, 1.60 M, 12.00 mmol) was
added via syringe and the reaction mixture was stirred for 15 minutes.
Then ZnBr2 [1.49 g, dissolved in dry diethyl ether (8.0 mL)] was added,
and the mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 30 mins, followed by addition
of ethyl glyoxylate (1.84 g, 9.00 mmol, 50% by wt, toluene solution). The
reaction mixture was warmed up to r. t. while stirring overnight.
Reaction was quenched with aq. saturated NH4Cl solution, and extracted
with diethyl ether (3 x 20 mL). The organic phases were combined, dried
over anhydrous MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo to give crude product.
Purification by silica gel column (5% EA/ Pet. Ether) gave 5b, yield 1.77
g, 86%. 1H NMR δ 0.10 (s , 6H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.6 Hz , 3H), 0.93 (s, 9H),
1.29 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.25-1.46 (m, 4H), 2.05 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H),
2.50-3.50 (br s, 1H), 4.15-4.30 (m, 2H), 4.30-4.45 (m, 2H), 4.93 (s, 1H),
5.58 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR δ -5.3, 13.9, 14.1, 18.3, 22.4, 25.9,
26.9, 30.2, 31.6, 59.8, 62.0, 69.5, 129.9, 137.0, 174.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Rapid Divergent Synthesis of Highly Substituted δ-Lactones
