$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 5a. 5a: To a solution of 2a
(149 mg, 0.5 mmol) in anhyd. THF (2.0 mL) under argon atmosphere was
added n-BuLi (0.22 mL of 2.5 M solution in hexane, 0.55 mmol) at -78 °C.
After stirring for 5 min, TMEDA (82 μL, 0.55 mmol) was added and the
resulting solution was warmed to -15 °C. A solution of benzyl bromide
(0.18 mL, 1.5 mmol) and anhyd. HMPA (0.35 mL, 2.0 mmol) in anhyd. THF
(0.5 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 6h at -15 °C
before quenched with aqueous HCl (1N, 1.0 mL). The mixture was extracted
with Et2O (3 × 5 mL). The combined organic layers were then dried over
Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The obtained crude
residue was dissolved in MeOH (1 mL), in which was added p-TsOH (17 mg,
0.1 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirring for 20 min and quenched with
sat. aq NaHCO3. After removing MeOH under reduced pressure, the mixture
was extracted with Et2O (3 × 5 mL). The combined organic layers were then
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification
of the crude residue via silica gel flash column chromatography (gradient
eluent: 0.5% of EtOAc/petroleum ether) afforded 5a (142 mg, 86%). [pure
5a-[γ/E]; other isomers containing 5a-[γ/Z] and 6a-[α]. Preparation of
5o. 5o: Using the same procedure as that used for 5a. 2d (64 mg, 0.3
mmol) in THF (1.3 mL) with phenyl lithium3 (0.45 mL of 1.0 M solution in
THF, 0.45 mmol), TMEDA (49 μL, 0.33 mmol), benzyl bromide (0.1 mL, 0.9
mmol) and anhyd. HMPA (0.21 mL, 1.2 mmol) at -15 °C for 6 h produced 5o
(66 mg) in 71% yield [pure 5o-[γ/E] (45 mg, 48%) as a yellow oil; other
isomers containing 5o-[γ/Z] and 6o-[α] (21 mg, 23%)] after silica gel
flash column chromatography (gradient eluent: 0.5% of EtOAc /petroleum
ether). 5o-[γ/E:Z], yield 72%; 6o-[α], yield 28%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 0.18 (s, 9H), 1.93 (d, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 2.18 (m, 1H), 2.43 (m, 1H),
2.60 (m, 2H), 5.16 (d, 1H, J = 2.4 Hz), 5.90 (s, 1H), 7.08 (d, 2H, J =
7.2 Hz), 7.16 (t, 1H, J = 7.2 Hz), 7.26 (m, 2H), 7.30 (m, 1H), 7.35-7.36
(m, 4H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.3, 35.1, 36.4, 78.1, 123.7, 125.9,
127.0, 127.9, 128.1, 128.4, 128.5, 141.9, 142.2, 158.3; IR (neat) cm-1
3392 (br, m), 3062 (m), 3027 (m), 2954 (s), 2929 (s), 2865 (s), 1616 (m),
1493 (m), 1453 (s), 1248 (s), 1035 (s), 837 (s), 748 (s), 699 (s); HRMS
(MALDI, m/z) calcd for C20H26OSiNa (M+Na)+: 333.1645, found 333.1651.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, [1,4]-Brook rearrangement (stage 1),
68:4 mixture of E and Z isomers obtained
