$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-hydroxy-1-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-2-butene (7a). To a
stirred solution of 3,5 dimethoxybenzaldehyde (1 g, 6.02 mmol) in dry THF
(20 mL), at 0°C, a solution of propenylmagnesium bromide (15 mL) in THF
was added dropwise. The reaction was stirred overnight, quenched with 10%
NH4Cl (aq) and extracted with ether (3 × 30mL). Organic part was washed
with water (2 × 20 mL) followed by brine and dried (MgSO4). The solution
was evaporated to dryness and the product was purified by silica gel
column chromatography eluting with 30% EtOAc-hexane. Yield 1.2g, (95%).
1-hydroxy-1-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-2-butene (7a). Yield 1.2g, (95%). 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.72 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H, minor isomer), 1.78 (d, J = 6.0
Hz, 2H, major isomer), 3.8 ( s, 6H), 5.07 (d, J = 6 Hz, 1H, minor
isomer), 5.5 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H, major isomer), 5.58-5.80 (m, 2H), 6.37 (
m, 1H), 6.54-6.57 ( m, 2H). HRMS (M+H) calcd. for C12H17O3: 209.1178;
found 209.1180. Compound 7a was reported but not well characterized in
the literature, e.g. reference 11. Therefore we reported 1H NMR and HRMS
data.
