$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure of
palladium/thioether-imidazolinium chloride system-catalyzed 1,2-addition
of aryl and alkenyl boronic acids to aldehydes. Under argon atmosphere, a
reaction tube was charged with [Pd(allyl)Cl]2 (0.0025-0.01mmol) , an
imidazolinium chloride (0.005-0.02mmol), and cesium fluoride (304 mg, 2
mmol), and then dioxane (2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred for 15
min at 80 °C and cooled to room temperature. Then, an aldehyde (1.0
mmol)and an organoboronic acid (1.5 mmol) were added, and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 80 °C.The mixture was cooled to room temperature,
and water and satd NH4Cl were added, and then, itwas extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were washed with brine, and then
driedover MgSO4. Concentration and purification through silica gel column
chromatography. (E)-2-Phenylethenyl-2-naphthylmethanol, yield 0.92 mmol,
92% . pale yellow solid, mp 79-80 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 2.11 (1H, d, J =
3.5 Hz), 5.57 (1H, dd, J = 3.5, 6.5 Hz),6.47 (1H, dd, J = 6.5, 16.0 Hz),
6.75 (1H, d, J = 16.0 Hz), 7.24 (1H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.31 (2H, t, J = 7.5
Hz), 7.41 (2H, d, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.46-7.51 (2H, m), 7.55 (1H, dd, J = 1.5,
8.5 Hz), 7.83-7.86 (3H, m), 7.90 (1H, s). 13C NMR (CDCl3): 75.2, 124.5,
124.9, 126.0,126.2, 126.6, 127.7, 127.8, 128.0, 128.4, 128.6, 130.8,
131.4, 133.0, 133.3, 136.5, 140.1. IR (nujol): 3280 cm-1. EIMS m/z: 260
(M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient 1,2-Addition of Aryl- and Alkenylboronic Acids to Aldehydes
Catalyzed by the Palladium/Thioether-Imidazolinium Chloride System
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kuriyama, Masami; Shimazawa, Rumiko; Shirai, Ryuichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(4), 1597-1600

