$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Optimized Conditions for Alkenylzinc Addition
to Aldehydes. A flame-dried vial was cooled to 0 °C and BH3- DMS (0.31
mL, 3.3 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (3 mL) was added, followed by cyclohexene (0.67
mL, 6.6 mmol). This solution was stirred at 0 °C for 2 h and appeared as
a white cloudy solution. Next, the alkyne (1.2 equiv, 3.6 mmol) was added
and the reaction was warmed to room temperature for 30 min yielding a
clear stock solution of vinylborane. Ligand 54 (13 mg, 0.019 mmol) was
combined with 2.0 M Me2Zn (0.16 mL, 0.32 mmol) in toluene at room
temperature for 5 min, then cooled to -78 °C, and the vinylborane stock
solution was added (approximately 0.37 mL or 1/12 the stock solution
volume depending on the alkyne used). After the reaction was stirred for
18 h at -78 °C, the appropriate aldehyde (0.25 mmol) was added and the
reaction was surrounded with dry ice and placed in a -20 °C freezer for
48 h. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl and diluted
with diethyl ether. The organic layer was washed with aqueous 1 N HCl (1
5 mL) and saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (1 5 mL). The solvent was removed and
the product was purified by column chromatography (8:92 EtOAc:hexanes).
(R,E)-(-)-4,4-Dimethyl-1-naphthalen-2-ylpent-2-en-1- ol, Allylic Alcohol
72. 91% ee by HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD-H column eluted with
hexanes:2-propanol (99.5:0.5) at 1.0 mL/min and detection at 219 nm), tR
) 68.7 min for (R) and tR ) 75.2 min for (S); [α]25D -52 (c 1.0, CHCl3);
mp 77-79 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.86 (m, 4 H), 7.49 (m, 3H), 5.88
(dd, J = 15.6, 0.7 Hz, 1 H), 5.66 (dd, J = 15.6, 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 5.35 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.01 (br s, 1 H), 1.06 (s, 9 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 144.2, 141.3, 133.8, 133.3, 128.6, 128.4, 128.1, 127.5, 126.5, 126.2,
125.0, 75.9, 33.4, 29.9; HRMSEI (M+) calcd for C17H20O 240.1514, found
240.1510.
